Interview Summary

If an interviewer asks what you've done so far, you can confidently say:

"I first developed an AI Memory Router that routes queries to RAG, Graph, or Tabular memory backends. Since Kubernetes is designed to run long-lived services rather than terminal applications, I converted the project into a REST API using FastAPI. I separated the AI logic from the API layer by introducing a reusable process_query() function and created HTTP endpoints to receive user queries and return structured JSON responses. I verified the API using FastAPI's Swagger UI, making the application ready for containerization with Docker and later deployment on Kubernetes."